aa, `beaten-natural-grouse`), not by this change. This change keeps the pins truthful. Committed as c984cedba41, stacked on 5c89609a0aa: 28 specs, `model:` line only. Strict validation unchanged (code-quality, gold-only, fails identically on origin/main). Before run (4.x, origin/main 872e7f6c3fd, gate-wrapped, REBAR_EVAL_MAX_CASES=12, 12:33 to 14:45 PST) is recorded; the after run follows on the stacked tree.","timestamp":1794267599942000001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Before/after evals (2026-11-09 PST)\n\nBefore: origin/main 872e7f6c3fd (Opus 4.8 / Sonnet 4.6). After: 0ed7010e9e7 (= 6f54ea438de, the upgrade with the reasoning-in-output fix, + spec pins). The later amend b76a747a4f3 adds only the prior-generation window table, which affects explicitly pinned 4.x ids, not 5.5 runs. Bedrock-first via AWS_PROFILE=frontier-bedrock. Prompt evals ran inside a local gate session (workaround for open bug dissocial-unpleasant-adouri; without it every case scores 0.00) at REBAR_EVAL_MAX_CASES=12, mirroring the eval-live loop. Provider parity: python -m rebar.llm.evals.provider_parity --concurrency 4, 50-item corpus, 3 epochs.\n\n```\nPROMPT EVALS (REBAR_EVAL_MAX_CASES=12)\nspec                                       4.x         5.5  5.5 failure messages\ncode-review-api-compat               FAIL 1.00   PASS 1.00  \ncode-review-base                     PASS 1.00   PASS 1.00  \ncode-review-concurrency              PASS 1.00   PASS 1.00  \ncode-review-db-migrations            FAIL 1.00   FAIL 1.00  3x false fire on a good case\ncode-review-docs                     FAIL 1.00   FAIL 1.00  3x false fire on a good case\ncode-review-failover                 PASS 1.00   PASS 1.00  \ncode-review-llm-prompts              FAIL 1.00   FAIL 1.00  2x false fire on a good case\ncode-review-performance              PASS 1.00   PASS 1.00  \ncode-review-security                 FAIL 1.00   FAIL 1.00  3x expected a finding/FAIL, got none\ncode-review-tests                    FAIL 1.00   FAIL 1.00  3x false fire on a good case\ncode-review-verify                   FAIL 1.00   FAIL 1.00  18x verifier emitted no `verifications`\ncompletion-verifier                  FAIL 1.00   FAIL 1.00  3x false fire on a good case\nplan-review-G7                       FAIL 1.00   FAIL 1.00  6x review result failed schema validation: 'dimension\nplan-review-T10                      PASS 1.00   PASS 1.00  \nplan-review-T15                      PASS 1.00   PASS 1.00  \nplan-review-ac-process-gate          FAIL 1.00   FAIL 1.00  2x review result failed schema validation: 'dimension\nplan-review-asserted-capability      FAIL 1.00   FAIL 1.00  5x review result failed schema validation: 'dimension\nplan-review-container                FAIL 0.00   FAIL 0.00  36x run error\nplan-review-decomp-shape             FAIL 1.00   FAIL 1.00  2x review result failed schema validation: 'dimension\nplan-review-evidence-kind            FAIL 1.00   FAIL 1.00  14x review result failed schema validation: 'dimension\nplan-review-finder                   FAIL 0.00   FAIL 0.00  36x run error\nplan-review-isf-finder               FAIL 0.00   FAIL 0.00  12x run error\nplan-review-necessity                FAIL 1.00   FAIL 1.00  2x review result failed schema validation: 'dimension\nplan-review-no-file-impact           FAIL 1.00   FAIL 1.00  3x review result failed schema validation: 'dimension\nplan-review-novelty                  PASS 1.00   PASS 1.00  \nplan-review-verifier                 FAIL 1.00   FAIL 1.00  36x no graded validity in verifier output; 36x no graded validity to discriminate on\nspec-alignment                       FAIL 1.00   PASS 1.00  \npassed: 4.x 7/27, 5.5 9/27\n\nPROVIDER PARITY\n4.x frontier invalid= False gating_failures= ['1 gold-regressing decision-level flip(s) on the gold set (must be 0)', 'false-accept rose 0.040 > margin 0.02']\n   agreement 0.98 flips 1 validity {'v1': 1.0, 'v2': 1.0} recall {'v1': 1.0, 'v2': 1.0} false_accept {'v1': 0.08, 'v2': 0.12} errors {'v1': 0, 'v2': 0} excluded 0\n4.x standard invalid= False gating_failures= []\n   agreement 1.0 flips 0 validity {'v1': 1.0, 'v2': 1.0} recall {'v1': 1.0, 'v2': 1.0} false_accept {'v1': 0.087, 'v2': 0.087} errors {'v1': 13, 'v2': 17} excluded 3\n5.5 frontier invalid= False gating_failures= []\n   agreement 1.0 flips 0 validity {'v1': 1.0, 'v2': 1.0} recall {'v1': 1.0, 'v2': 1.0} false_accept {'v1': 0.04, 'v2': 0.04} errors {'v1': 0, 'v2': 0} excluded 0\n5.5 standard invalid= False gating_failures= ['1 gold-regressing decision-level flip(s) on the gold set (must be 0)']\n   agreement 0.98 flips 1 validity {'v1': 1.0, 'v2': 1.0} recall {'v1': 0.96, 'v2': 0.96} false_accept {'v1': 0.08, 'v2': 0.0} errors {'v1': 0, 'v2': 0} excluded 0\n```\n\nReading: no spec regressed from PASS to FAIL; code-review-api-compat and spec-alignment moved FAIL to PASS. Every spec failing on 5.5 fails identically on 4.x: three have no solver (bug knightly-salty-orangutan, coverage 0.00 on both), seven plan-review specs fail schema validation on a 'dimension' field on both, and the rest are false-fire/miss gates on both. Parity: both 5.5 slots are invalid=false with zero sampling_parameter/auth_validation errors (the 4.x standard slot had 13+17 step-budget/runaway errors; 5.5 has none). The 5.5 standard slot has 1 gold-regressing flip (ELE-F1, block on direct, advisory on Bedrock; one gold-improving flip NETMECH-F1 the other way), so it does not meet the 0-flip parity bar; the 4.x frontier slot failed the same bar with 1 flip plus a false-accept rise. A single 3-epoch run cannot separate model change from run-to-run noise at n=50.\n\nPushed as Gerrit change 3341 (WIP), patch set 1 = 3b8bf2f94de62c8d340849e6de048114b136f1a9, stacked on 3340. make verify exited 0 (17:58 to 18:26 PST; 20,891 + 202 passed). The amend added the one test that pins a spec's model value (test_evidence_kind_criterion); file impact updated and plan re-reviewed: PASS, signed 18:05 PST.","timestamp":1794277636988409001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Change 3341 PS1 got Verified -1 (CI run 42742825985): test_review_bot.py::test_shutdown_drains_an_in_flight_reconciler_review timed out at its 3.0s probe cap. Unrelated to this change (eval-spec model: lines only); the same test failed on an unrelated run on 2026-11-03. Filed as bug alphabetic-reluctant-dore. Not rechecked: AGENTS.md allows recheck only for provably environmental faults. 3341 is held pending an operator decision.","timestamp":1794280282882811001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"HANDOFF STATE 2026-11-09 19:52 PST: in_progress, plan certified. Change 3341 PS1 3b8bf2f94de62c8d340849e6de048114b136f1a9 is ready (not WIP) with LLM-Review +1 and Verified -1 (flaky test_shutdown_drains_an_in_flight_reconciler_review, bug alphabetic-reluctant-dore; not rechecked). Its parent 3340 has merged. Worktree .rebar/worktrees/spec-pins-55b @ 3b8bf2f94de, clean. Next: resolve the CI failure or get an operator-authorized recheck, land at the current SHA with gerrit_safe_submit.py, tick the AC boxes, then close.","timestamp":1794282807178012001},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"PROGRESS 2026-11-10 20:16 PST (session 3d705fec): The flake that blocked 3341 (alphabetic-reluctant-dore) is fixed, merged as 02e86fe67db, and closed. 3341 was rebased in .rebar/worktrees/spec-pins-55b onto origin/main 02e86fe (rebase --onto, dropping the stale pre-merge parent b76a747) and is now e6bcff4b9c48b1bc50826d878f0f2764d082b97d, with the same Change-Id I53d1bc8d and the same 29-file diff. make verify passed (19:38–20:14 PST, rc 0: 20,910 + 202 tests passed). It was pushed as a new patchset of 3341, and fresh votes are pending.","timestamp":1794370515340723570},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"LANDED 2026-11-10 20:41 PST: Gerrit change 3341 reached LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 with 0 unresolved comments at revision e6bcff4b9c48b1bc50826d878f0f2764d082b97d (votes observed 20:41 PST). It was submitted with scripts/gerrit_safe_submit.py at that revision. Gerrit rebased it server-side onto 9f8b2af21c8 and merged it to main as 0f02c333bfea741ce00bbafba64e63ae87b92859 (\"Move eval-spec model pins to the 5.5 ids\"). Status: MERGED.\n\nAC evidence on main at 0f02c333:\n1. `git grep -nE 'claude-(opus-4-8|sonnet-4-6|haiku-4-5)' -- 'src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/*.eval.yaml'` prints nothing (rc 1).\n2. The before/after prompt-eval summaries are in the \"Before/after evals (2026-11-09 PST)\" comment.\n3. make verify exited 0 on e6bcff4b (19:38–20:14 PST: 20,910 + 202 passed), and earlier on PS1 3b8bf2f9.","timestamp":1794372340444777839},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"HANDOFF STATE 2026-11-10 PST (session 3d705fec): CLOSED. The completion verifier passed and signed at 0f02c333bfea741ce00bbafba64e63ae87b92859.\n- Change 3341 merged as 0f02c333 (submitted 20:41 PST).\n- AC boxes were ticked with no other description change, so the plan review stayed certified (checked with plan_review_status).\n- The close used ref=0f02c333 because the MCP server's /var/gerrit/site/mcp-code is still at 3835269d792, the workspace lag tracked on epic pompous-vitriolic-macaw.\n- Worktree .rebar/worktrees/spec-pins-55b sits at 0f02c333 with nothing pending.","timestamp":1794372787163236137}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1794256006727331001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"69837cc0-e5ff-4d47-b7e9-9d9721a3b036","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7341-7f22-b13a-442c"},{"link_uuid":"ba230756-467c-44c9-b4a6-c67a05de1a6a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"83d6-ce35-33a6-40b3"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nEach prompt-eval spec in `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/*.eval.yaml` pins the model it generates with in a top-level `model:` key (for example `plan-review-finder.eval.yaml:11` is `anthropic:claude-opus-4-8`; `plan-review-evidence-kind.eval.yaml:5` is `bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6`), read by `rebar.llm.evals.eval` at `eval.py:308` (`gen_model = spec.get(\"model\")`). After the configured models move to the 5.5 generation (sibling task `beaten-natural-grouse`), these pins would keep the prompt evals measuring the retired models, so the evals could not show whether the prompts still pass on the models that actually run.\n\n## Approach\n\nMove every spec pin to the 5.5 id of the same family and provider, keeping the provider each spec names: `anthropic:claude-opus-4-8` to `anthropic:claude-opus-5-5`, `anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6` to `anthropic:claude-sonnet-5-5`, `bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6` to `bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5`, and any Haiku pin to `claude-haiku-5-5`. Run the prompt evals the `eval-live` job defines (`.github/workflows/prompt-eval.yml`: `rebar.llm.evals.eval.run_eval` over each dataset-bearing spec at `REBAR_EVAL_MAX_CASES=12`) once on the 4.x pins before the change and once on the 5.5 pins after, with `AWS_PROFILE=frontier-bedrock`, and record both summaries (spec, pass/fail, coverage) as a ticket comment. The commit is stacked on the upgrade task's commit (Gerrit parent), so it cannot land first, and the after-run is made on that stack because the 5.5 request-surface fixes (no temperature, explicit effort, corrected profile) must be in place for it to be meaningful; a one-to-one family mapping keeps each spec measuring the same tier it was calibrated on.\n\n## Scope\n\n- src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/*.eval.yaml (the `model:` line of each spec that pins a 4.x model; no other line changes)\n\n## Testing\n\n- `tests/unit` eval-discipline checks (the offline tier `_eval-discipline.yml` runs) pass, so spec validation still accepts every edited file.\n- Live: the before and after prompt-eval runs described above.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `git grep -nE 'claude-(opus-4-8|sonnet-4-6|haiku-4-5)' -- src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/*.eval.yaml` prints nothing.\n- [x] The before (4.x) and after (5.5) prompt-eval summaries are recorded in a ticket comment, one line per spec with pass/fail and coverage.\n- [x] `make verify` exits 0.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/code-quality.eval.yaml","reason":"model pin to 5.5"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/code-review-api-compat.eval.yaml","reason":"model pin to 5.5"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/code-review-base.eval.yaml","reason":"model pin to 5.5"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/code-review-concurrency.eval.yaml","reason":"model pin to 5.5"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/code-review-db-migrations.eval.yaml","reason":"model pin to 5.5"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/code-review-docs.eval.yaml","reason":"model pin to 5.5"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/code-review-failover.eval.yaml","reason":"model pin to 5.5"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/code-review-llm-prompts.eval.yaml","reason":"model pin to 5.5"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/code-review-performance.eval.yaml","reason":"model pin to 5.5"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/code-review-security.eval.yaml","reason":"model pin to 5.5"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/code-review-tests.eval.yaml","reason":"model pin to 5.5"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/code-review-verify.eval.yaml","reason":"model pin to 5.5"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/completion-verifier.eval.yaml","reason":"model pin to 5.5"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-T10.eval.yaml","reason":"model pin to 5.5"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-T15.eval.yaml","reason":"model pin to 5.5"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-ac-process-gate.eval.yaml","reason":"model pin to 5.5"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-asserted-capability.eval.yaml","reason":"model pin to 5.5"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-container.eval.yaml","reason":"model pin to 5.5"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-decomp-shape.eval.yaml","reason":"model pin to 5.5"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-evidence-kind.eval.yaml","reason":"model pin to 5.5"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-finder.eval.yaml","reason":"model pin to 5.5"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-g7.eval.yaml","reason":"model pin to 5.5"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-isf-finder.eval.yaml","reason":"model pin to 5.5"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-necessity.eval.yaml","reason":"model pin to 5.5"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-no-file-impact.eval.yaml","reason":"model pin to 5.5"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-novelty.eval.yaml","reason":"model pin to 5.5"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-verifier.eval.yaml","reason":"model pin to 5.5"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/spec-alignment.eval.yaml","reason":"model pin to 5.5"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_evidence_kind_criterion.py","reason":"test pinning a spec model value"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["parent","9794-4336-5ed6-4561"],["relates_to","7341-7f22-b13a-442c"],["relates_to","83d6-ce35-33a6-40b3"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"9794-4336-5ed6-4561","parent_status_uuid":"27497654-64bb-4b30-a307-77311e91cf66","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"81a1-0fc3-496d-4a00","ticket_type":"task","title":"Move prompt-eval spec model pins to the 5.5 ids and record before/after prompt evals","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["111c319a-7a22-44